Problem Observables couldn’t solve alone
Scenario:
“I want to manually push values and share them with many subscribers”
Observable alone ❌:
// You cannot call next() from outside

Subject solves this
const subject = new Subject<number>();
Subject is:
Observable (can subscribe) + 
Observer (has next())
📌 Acts like an event emitter
Example
const subject = new Subject<number>();

subject.subscribe(v => console.log('A', v));
subject.subscribe(v => console.log('B', v));

subject.next(1);
subject.next(2);

Output:
A 1
B 1
A 2
B 2

What is a Subject (in one line)

👉 Subject = Observable + Observer
You can emit values using next()
You can subscribe to it like an Observable
It does NOT store any value

Key rules of Subject
✔ No initial value
✔ Emits values only to current subscribers
❌ Does NOT replay old values
❌ Late subscribers miss previous emissions

