EX: why last subscriber miss value:
Code example (step-by-step)
        import { Subject } from 'rxjs';
        const subject = new Subject<number>();
        // Subscriber 1
        subject.subscribe(value => {
          console.log('Subscriber 1:', value);
        });
        subject.next(1);
        subject.next(2);
        // Subscriber 2 (LATE)
        subject.subscribe(value => {
          console.log('Subscriber 2:', value);
        });
        subject.next(3);

        🔍 Output
        Subscriber 1: 1
        Subscriber 1: 2
        Subscriber 1: 3
        Subscriber 2: 3

5️⃣ WHY late subscribers miss old values?
Behind the scenes 🧠
Subject does not store emitted values
When you call next(value):
It immediately pushes the value to currently subscribed observers
If no one is listening → value is lost forever

